abstract: "A theoretical and synthetic-computational analysis of identifiability limits when epigenetic-clock changes may include direct marker effects. The release contains a reproducible synthetic benchmark and a constrained information-gain design planner. It makes no empirical rejuvenation or lifespan-extension claim."
keywords:
  - epigenetic clocks
  - causal identifiability
  - active experimental design
  - aging biomarkers
  - synthetic benchmark
